##  switch statement and expression
https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/23/language/switch-expressions-and-statements.html#GUID-560486C0-1815-4DC2-B7BD-39FF96C99943

PYS rules (locked):
- No implicit fall-through. Trailing `continue` in a case body falls through.
- `break` is not required (not part of the teaching surface).
- Statement form: `case L: …`  Expression form: `case L, M => expr` (RHS-assignable).
- Do not mix `:` and `=>` in one switch.
- Subjects: enums and equality-comparable primitives (int/widths, string, char, bool, …).
- Bare enum labels (`MONDAY`) resolve when the subject type is that enum.
- Expression: exhaustiveness required (all enum members or `default`; non-enum needs `default`).
- Statement: non-exhaustive without `default` → warning.
/#

enum Day {
    MONDAY
    FRIDAY
    SUNDAY
    TUESDAY
    THURSDAY
    SATURDAY
    WEDNESDAY
}
int numLetters = 0
Day day = Day.WEDNESDAY

switch (day) {
    case MONDAY:
        continue
    case FRIDAY:
        continue
    case SUNDAY:
        numLetters = 6
    case TUESDAY:
        continue
    case THURSDAY:
        numLetters = 7
    case SATURDAY:
        numLetters = 8
    case WEDNESDAY:
        numLetters = 9
}

print(numLetters)

# same effect but as an expression

numLetters =  switch (day) {
    case MONDAY, SUNDAY, FRIDAY => 6
    case TUESDAY, THURSDAY => 7
    case SATURDAY => 8
    case WEDNESDAY => 9
}
print(numLetters)
